From 8f31f6f2f0f1f25d6cbb6a8142dd786f6a5d8b35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChatGPT <patches@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH v3] hydrogenx: fuse schedutil-style boost, input scenes and fs/zram configs

Add HydrogenX v3 for pissarro/MT6877 Android 4.14 kernels.

This is a cumulative patch intended for a clean update-to-357 tree.  It keeps
schedutil available, makes hydrogenx the default governor, adds a global
/sys/kernel/hydrogenx scene controller, wires automatic input boosts into the
input subsystem, and enables common f2fs/erofs/zram/compression/network
configuration symbols in the pissarro defconfigs.

The MTK GPU/DDR/IO and SchedTune/UCLAMP entry points are weak bridge symbols:
when a vendor tree exports matching strong symbols the bridge uses them; when
it does not, the patch still builds and the cpufreq/input side remains active.
