+	depends on SMP
+	select CPU_FREQ_GOV_HYDROGENX
+	select CPU_FREQ_GOV_PERFORMANCE
+	help
+	  Use the 'hydrogenx' CPUFreq governor by default.
+
+	  This governor is tuned for Android phones that need fast response
+	  under UI/game bursts, but also need slower ramp-down and optional
+	  powersave bias to reduce frequency bouncing and heat.
+	  The fallback governor will be 'performance'.
 
 endchoice
@@ -148,6 +161,28 @@ config CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL
 
 	  If in doubt, say N.
+
+config CPU_FREQ_GOV_HYDROGENX
+	bool "'hydrogenx' cpufreq policy governor"
+	depends on CPU_FREQ && SMP
+	select CPU_FREQ_GOV_COMMON
+	help
+	  'hydrogenx' is a third-party Android-oriented dynamic cpufreq
+	  governor.  It uses the common dbs governor framework, and v3 can
+	  read the global HydrogenX boost scene controller for input, frame,
+	  GPU, DDR and IO boost floors.
+
+	  The policy prefers:
+	  - fast ramp-up when CPU load crosses up_threshold;
+	  - schedutil-like fast reaction via boost floors;
+	  - a configurable hispeed floor for frame-sensitive loads;
+	  - delayed ramp-down through min_sample_time to reduce FPS jitter;
+	  - optional powersave_bias for lower heat and power at light load;
+	  - userspace boostpulse support for game/touch/performance daemons.
+
+	  Tunables are exported below the governor sysfs directory and global
+	  boost scene knobs are under /sys/kernel/hydrogenx/.
+
+	  If in doubt, say N.
 
 comment "CPU frequency scaling drivers"

